course: dictionary
lesson: 10133
title: Threatened: in danger
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Threatened is the past form of the verb threaten. To threaten someone is to say or show that you will hurt them, or that something bad may happen. «Most kinds of lemurs are endangered, mainly because their forests are being cut down, and they are among the most threatened mammals in the world.» The clues are endangered and forests being cut down, so threatened means in danger.
explain: Threatened can also be an adjective that describes a person or animal. If you feel threatened, you feel unsafe, and you should move to a safe place and tell an adult. In a story, a threatened character may run, hide or fight back.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The most threatened mammals» can become «the mammals most in danger of dying out», and it still makes sense, so you have got it.
fact: Threaten means to say or show that you will do something bad to someone, or that something bad may happen.
fact: «Threatened» is the past form of threaten, and it can also be an adjective meaning in danger or unsafe.
fact: A threatened animal or plant is in danger of dying out.
fact: «Threatened species» are animals and plants at risk because of hunting, pollution or loss of their homes.
fact: The IUCN Red List records how endangered each species is, and «more than 47,000 species on it are judged threatened.»
exercise: «Most kinds of lemurs are endangered, mainly because their forests are being cut down, and they are among the most threatened mammals in the world.» What does threatened mean here? | Found only in cold places | *In danger of dying out | Very friendly and happy | Good at climbing trees
exercise: Tom felt threatened when the stranger shouted at him in the dark. What does threatened mean? | *Feeling in danger or unsafe | Feeling bored and sleepy | Feeling very proud | Feeling warm and cosy
exercise: «The threatened turtle was moved to a safe pond.» What does threatened suggest about the turtle? | It was very large and heavy | It was hungry for lunch | It was asleep in the sun | *It was in danger of dying out
test: «The rhino is threatened by hunters.» Which words are the clue that threatened means in danger? | *Hunters are after it | It lives in a big field | It is grey | The rhino is
test: In a story, what does a threatened character most likely feel? | *Afraid and in danger | Cold and wet | Sleepy after lunch | Bored
exam: Which sentence uses threatened to mean in danger of dying out? | Lily threatened a big smile at the party | *The panda was threatened, so people began to protect its forest | The bus threatened to be late | He threatened to tell on me, so I stayed quiet
